  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Maintains a comprehensive NHS free at point of need; at least £540m extra annually for health and £200m for frontline staff; restore free eye and dental checks; freeze prescription charges; maximum six‑month wait from diagnosis to treatment; build more affordable homes and end rough sleeping by 2000; national home insulation prioritising low‑income households; raise tax thresholds for low earners; earnings‑linked top‑up for low‑income pensioners; regionally variable minimum wage; extensive anti‑discrimination measures for women, disabled people, ethnic minorities and LGBT; stronger victim support; investment in schools, early years, and SEN; childcare strategy and parental leave. TEXT_G: Calls for a referendum on Europe focused on sovereignty versus a federal Europe; urgency due to constitutional change; emphasizes public consent and Parliament’s role in wording; contrasts with parties’ focus on single currency.",
